#8. Summary paragraphs

The Chinese banking sector is in the early stages of Japaneseization, but ** the whole does not amount to a share. At the NIM 1.42%, ROE 8%, and PB 0.5-0.7 'Down tide', the industry Beta was negative but Alpha’s opportunities were magnified.** Currently, it is one of the best banking stock allocation windows in the last 10 years – provided that the banks are selected**.

** The only Chinese bank to be engaged in a three-pronged process of "business model plus management plus governance structure"** its AUM + low-cost call-back loops are expected to be able to match the model of rich country banks; Ningpo Bank, although excellent, has a management replacement period of 1-2 years to observe; construction/business banks are "bond-type" with 5% plus dividends but are not growing enough; and booming, safe, transportation is entering the "value trap" risk zone due to transition difficulties/house-traffic openings/capital pressures.

** The discipline of Dong-Juan's "PE> 15-fold sale"** is the most operational part of its methodology – which means that bank equity investments are ** "value repair + dividends compound", not "long-term ten-year share". Under the dual support of policy beta (medium-value valuation + market value management + risk management) and basic gamma (recruitment/Ningpo Bay River), 20-30% of the value repair space is left in the next 1-2 years, but ** it is important to be vigilant about the value killing under the Japanese conversion path (40% probability)** - even if ROE is only slightly down at that time, PB may be cut.

** Final recommendation**: Use the "business model certainty" employed x "earlier cash flow" of State-owned majors x strict "pe 15 times more discipline" to build a Chinese portfolio of bank shares.** Avoid "medium banking" and "high dividends trap" and "under-disclosed house."**

